# go.sum is deliberately NOT ignored. A library must commit it: without it,
# `go build` fails for anyone who clones the repo, and module checksums cannot be
# verified. It was previously listed here, which left the repository unbuildable
# from a fresh clone.

# Test and profiling artifacts. `go test` leaves the compiled binary behind
# whenever a -cpuprofile / -memprofile flag is used.
*.test
*.out
*.prof

# Generated knowledge-graph output: 4 MB of regenerable artifacts, plus state
# holding absolute paths to one machine's Python install. GRAPH_REPORT.md is the
# exception — it is small, human-readable, and worth reviewing in a diff.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/GRAPH_REPORT.md

# Editor and OS noise
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store

# Build artifacts from `go build ./...` in a main package
/examples/gpoolproxy/gpoolproxy
